A realistic value-normalizing guard where type checks meet: a misspelled
LimsTypeEx result, a code block compared with ==, a number tested with
$, a string literal = (info), and :Format with a scalar second argument
instead of an array. The NUMERIC branch with the {} Format form is
correct.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE NormalizeValue;
	:PARAMETERS vValue, fnDefault, nCode;
	:DECLARE sFmt, sOut;
	sFmt := "value={0}";
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "NUMERIC";
		sOut := sFmt:Format("n={0}", {LimsString(vValue)});
		:EXITCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "STRING";
		sOut := sFmt:Format("s={0}", AllTrim(vValue));
		:EXITCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "BOOLEAN";
		sOut := IIF(vValue, "yes", "no");
		:EXITCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		:IF fnDefault == NIL .OR. nCode $ "123";
			sOut := "";
		:ELSE;
			sOut := Eval(fnDefault, vValue);
		:ENDIF;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;
	:IF sOut = "value";
		sOut := sOut + "=";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE NormalizeValue;
	:PARAMETERS vValue, fnDefault, nCode;
	:DECLARE sFmt, sOut;

	sFmt := "value={0}";

	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "NUMERIC";
		sOut := sFmt:Format("n={0}", {LimsString(vValue)});
		:EXITCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "STRING";
		sOut := sFmt:Format("s={0}", AllTrim(vValue));
		:EXITCASE;
	:CASE LimsTypeEx(vValue) == "BOOLEAN";
		sOut := IIf(vValue, "yes", "no");
		:EXITCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		:IF fnDefault == NIL .OR. nCode $ "123";
			sOut := "";
		:ELSE;
			sOut := Eval(fnDefault, vValue);
		:ENDIF;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;

	:IF sOut = "value";
		sOut := sOut + "=";
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
10:32-10:47 warning format_arg_not_array: sFmt:Format takes ONE array holding every replacement value - wrap the values in braces: sFmt:Format(template, {...})
12:30-12:39 error invalid_limstypeex_comparison: LimsTypeEx never returns "BOOLEAN" - this comparison can never be true. Valid results (uppercase, compared case-sensitively): NIL, STRING, NUMERIC, LOGIC, DATE, ARRAY, CODEBLOCK, OBJECT, SSLVALUE
16:17-16:19 warning code_block_comparison: Code blocks (lambdas) cannot be compared with '=='. This causes an error
16:35-16:36 warning dollar_string_only: The '$' containment operator only works on strings. Non-string operands cause error
